<section>
    <p class="eyebrow">Step 2</p>
    <h3>Enable the recorder in the test environment</h3>
    <pre><code class="language-yaml" data-trim>
# config/packages/http_client.yaml
when@test:
    http_client:
        recorder: true
    </code></pre>
    <p class="fragment callout">
        The recorder decorates <code>http_client.transport</code>, as close to the network as possible:
        <b>all</b> clients (default and scoped) are recorded, with absolute URLs, in a single file per test.
    </p>
    <p class="fragment callout warn">
        Without this line, <code>#[UseRecord]</code> has no client to drive: the test hits the network.
    </p>
    <aside class="notes">
        Since Symfony 8.2, the HTTP client configuration lives in HttpClientBundle: the root key is http_client, no longer framework. The recorder is opt-in: for a short while it was enabled automatically in the test environment, but Nicolas removed that, it would have been a first in the Symfony codebase. Nothing changes in the application code. Without the attribute on the test, and outside PHPUnit, it is in passthrough mode.
    </aside>
</section>
